like so many other parts of the world  this area nowadays called the Islamic  Republic of Iran has gone by many names  by far the most famous of these names is  Persia this name actually comes from a  misunderstanding  in which the administrative region of  the Achaemenid Empire Persis or pass was  mistaken for the name of the entire  empire they shouldn't be too surprising  given at those who gave them this name  often named their empires in the same  way also in case you're wondering this  was also where the name for the Iranian  language Farsi comes from now Persia  wasn't the name that the people of the  Persian Empire used to describe it and  they often used area Iran or a rancher  to refer to it which means of the Aryans  the name given to the people who lived  there and not you know those other guys  ancient Iran isn't the same as the  modern nation of Iran and has been a  name used by many peoples from Syria to  Afghanistan to describe the area that  they lived in now native names for a  nation aren't often the ones used by  outsiders just a skosh land or junk war  unlike Germany or China the name for  Iran has changed in by formal  correspondence and everyday  communication so when did this change  occur when did the majority of people  start calling Persia Iran well the  change was a fairly recent one coming  about in 1935 when the Shah of Iran Reza  Shah demanded that everyone stopped  calling at Persia and start calling it  well Iran Reza Shah was a nationalist in  the sense that he wanted to make Iran a  more unified centralized state something  made harder by the fact that everyone  outside the nation called it in its  people by the wrong name as such Reza  Shah whilst at the League of Nations  formally asked all of the nations to  refer to his kingdom as Iran and that  continuing to call it Persia would be  seen as disrespectful  now some countries like the United  States in Nazi Germany were pretty quick  at taking on these changes whereas  others were not so quick and by others I  mean pretty much exclusively the United  Kingdom formally there were some changes  at this point such as the anglo-persian  oil company being renamed to the  anglo-iranian oil company however at the  highest levels that the British  government it was still known as Persia  because old habits and all that British  governors and bureaucrats often mr.  Quran for simply being a misspelling or  variation of Iraq and so correspondents  started to get mixed up when Reza Shahs  successor Mohammad Reza Shah came to  London he was originally going to be  given the title of Shah of Iran except  that the serving British Prime Minister  Winston Churchill didn't like Iran's new  name and so demanded that it be changed  which it was much to the annoyance of  many Iranian diplomats as for Mohammad  a Shah himself he didn't really care and  said both names were perfectly  acceptable that said momentum was on  Iran's side in by the mid-1970s the name  change it finely filtered down to all  countries and the British government was  successfully referring to Iran as Iran  and so afterwards Persia would forever  after lose its contemporary meaning and  would only be attached to an empire that  hadn't existed for roughly 1400 years I  hope you enjoyed this episode and thank  you for watching me thanks to my patreon  supporters whom you can see on screen  now plus with an extra special thanks to  James Bissonnette Danny Maloney coolin  Castleman party boy Co Rob Waterhouse Mo  Aaron the white Michael Reynolds Chris  wicker Gustav Swan Ashwin Emperor Gareth  Turner David Silverman spinning three  plates  Maggie packs Kowski Christian check a  Spencer Lightfoot  Winston K word Anthony Beckett Kelly  moneymaker  Robert Wetzel Lexi Schwinn Skye Chappell  and Ike
 

